; rungs/respond-defence-weak.eval - the LOW arm of the `taken` pair.
;
; PARTNER FILE: rungs/respond-defence-strong.eval. THE ONLY LINE THAT MAY DIFFER
; BETWEEN THEM IS THE `spawn` — everything else must stay identical or the pair
; stops being an A/B. They are two files rather than one shared fragment because
; the knob is on the MONSTER, and the monster is spawned inside the encounter;
; the offence pair shares one fragment precisely because its knob is on the party
; and can be set before the sweep.
;
; Why the monster and not the party's armour, which would have shared a fragment:
; measured, `wear plate_cuirass` + `avoid 8` moved `taken` by 17% against an x3
; monster, and at x1.5 and x2 the effect was smaller than the sample noise and
; sometimes inverted. Soak is flat, so it matters least against exactly the heavy
; blows a self-test needs in order to be reliable. A subtle knob makes a flaky
; check (docs/eval-audit.md, Tier 3 item 10).

heal
arena open 9 9
freeze off
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south 2
tp 14 12
tally reset
step 20
tally
